00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.370 align:start position:0%
in a historic move Northern California  voters have recalled a judge from office  over a controversial sentencing decision  The Associated Press projects that  nearly 60% of voters in Santa Clara  County chose to remove Judge Aaron  Persky he's the first California judge  to be recalled in 86 years Persky was  targeted for giving a short jail  sentence to brock Turner a former  Stanford University swimmer convicted of  sexual assault with the intent to commit  rape John Blackstone is in Palo Alto  California with reaction to the vote  John good morning good morning well this  case drew outrage from around the world  but the recall raised questions of  judicial independence now the final vote  tally won't be in for days probably but  as soon as the counting started last  night the trend was obvious judge Persky  was likely to lose his job here at the  Santa Clara County Superior Court women  are standing up and saying enough is  enough it was a night of victories for  Stanford Law Professor Michelle Dawber  who led a campaign for nearly two years  to remove Judge Aaron Persky from the  bench sexual violence and violence  against women is a voting issue Dawber  harnessed widespread anger over Persky  sentencing of brock Turner Turner was  freed from County Jail after serving  just three months of his six month  sentence for sexually assaulting a woman  following a fraternity party at Stanford  her searing statement about the impact  of sexual assault was read to Turner in  court and widely shared I accept  responsibility for every decision that  I've made as a judge in his only  television interview before the recall  vote Persky defended the sentence you  did have some idea before you passed the  sentence that it would be a  controversial sentence yes and by my  ethical constraints by the rule of law I  had to completely tune that out persky's  supporters insisted judges should not be  held hostage to public opinion this  recall is a very serious threat to do  retired Superior Court judge ladoris  Cordell campaign to keep Persky on the  bench  they're targeting a judge with no  history or track record of bias who did  nothing wrong and made a lawful decision  and they have succeeded in taking his  job away but Dawber stands by her  campaign  Tuesday night she ended it with the  words Turner's victim read in court two  girls everywhere we are with you on  nights when you feel alone we are with  you  Cordell said she spoke with Persky last  night and while he's disappointed with  the outcome he's doing ok she said he's  a licensed lawyer and he can practice  law but she worries that this vote sends  a message to judges everywhere that if  you do your job and people don't like it  you could be fired John John Blackstone  thanks
 

